                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="2" value="&lt;h1&gt;WIP Notes:&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;want to do an update-in-place type of edit option, instead of putting the data into the existing add-data fields.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;On that note, do the same for adding. Click (+) button &amp;gt; new line added &amp;gt; edit data &amp;gt; On blur, save the data || &amp;gt;if error, highlight errors, if user presses esc or (X) then clear the line&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Data should be added with the 'end date' being the last payment date. don't know why I thought it should be the other way around. V odd.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Gotta start working on the first-draft of the API aswell. That atleast, should be fun. Should probably do it in python to really cement the syntax into my head for work&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Also, gotta start using some kind of agile board for this stuff. &amp;gt; Number &amp;gt; Go &amp;gt; Up&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Also also, clean up the codebase and make nicer UI. IT's _ok_ right now, but it could be soooo much nicer&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#6F0000;fillColor=#a20025;spacing=5;spacingTop=-20;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;fontColor=#ffffff;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1079" y="80" width="324" height="440" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
            </root>
        </mxGraphModel>
    </diagram>
</mxfile>